v1.7
  Leaves other drivers' serial ports alone. The transmitter is looked for on
  CH340, FTDI and CP210x adapters, because that is what Arduino boards use -
  but so does everything else on a GX device. Measured on a Cerbo with an
  Autoterm heater on an FTDI: five Venus services probing the same port cut
  the heater driver from 29 answers out of 29 to 2 out of 30. This driver
  would have caused exactly that every minute, because a candidate port that
  did not answer was handed back to serial-starter - including one another
  driver had just claimed for itself.

  serial-starter keeps a node under /dev/serial-starter for every tty it still
  manages, and a driver claiming a port removes it. A candidate without that
  node is therefore not free but taken, and is now skipped entirely: not
  probed, not stopped, not handed back. A freshly plugged in Arduino is always
  under serial-starter, so nothing that should be found is lost. Where the
  directory does not exist - not a GX, or an older Venus - everything works as
  before.

